---
import ContentCard from '../../components/ContentCard.astro';
import DocumentLayout from '../../layouts/DocumentLayout.astro';
import { absoluteUrl, seo } from '../../data/seo';

const meta = seo.schemas;
const siteUrl = Astro.site?.toString() || 'https://tensor-standards.pages.dev/';
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'TechArticle',
  headline: meta.title,
  description: meta.description,
  url: absoluteUrl(siteUrl, meta.canonicalPath),
};
---

<DocumentLayout title={meta.title} description={meta.description} canonicalPath={meta.canonicalPath} ogType={meta.ogType} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <ContentCard>
<p class="section-kicker">Versioned data formats</p>
    <h2>Core record schemas</h2>
    <p>Core <strong>0.1.0-draft.1</strong> provides JSON Schemas for bundles, definitions, and records. The semantic validator additionally checks references, definition pins, context, and transition selections.</p>
    <ul><li><a href="/core/0.1.0-draft.1/schemas/bundle.schema.json" download>Bundle schema</a> — record and attached exact definition artifacts.</li><li><a href="/core/0.1.0-draft.1/schemas/definition.schema.json" download>Definition schema</a> — questions, parameters, criteria, and transitions.</li><li><a href="/core/0.1.0-draft.1/schemas/record.schema.json" download>Record schema</a> — investigation context, entries, references, and history.</li></ul>
    <p><a href="/read/core/0.1.0-draft.1/binding/">Binding rules</a> · <a href="/read/core/0.1.0-draft.1/coverage/">Validation coverage</a> · <a href="/implement/">Implementation guide</a></p>
    <h2>Published graph schema</h2>
    <p>The graph schema describes nodes, edges, and namespaced graph extensions. It is the format used by the published release and Graph Studio, separate from the Core definition-and-record format.</p>
    <ul><li><a href="/assets/data/core.schema.json" download>Graph Studio schema · 0.20260206e</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/TENSOR-Standards-Consortium/TENSOR-Framework/tree/main/releases/core/schemas">Published schema archive</a></li></ul>
    <p><a href="/extensions/">Graph layer formats and examples</a> · <a href="/questions/">Published question catalog</a></p>
    <h2>Artifact identity</h2>
    <p>Reproducible references include an explicit version and exact content digest. The Core <a href="/core/0.1.0-draft.1/provenance.json">provenance manifest</a> and <a href="/review/current/manifest.json">review manifest</a> publish the relevant source identities and hashes.</p>
  </ContentCard>
</DocumentLayout>
